			"versionNonce": 786474677,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783350667405,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "We also have specific names for the first and the last node in the list. \nWe call the first node “HEAD” and the last node “TAIL”. \nAs you see above, tail node points to a null value, which means Linked Lists are\n“null terminated”. \nIn simpler words, this is how we know we are at the end of a Linked List.",
			"rawText": "We also have specific names for the first and the last node in the list. \nWe call the first node “HEAD” and the last node “TAIL”. \nAs you see above, tail node points to a null value, which means Linked Lists are “null terminated”. \nIn simpler words, this is how we know we are at the end of a Linked List.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "hS-S7sbP186sIEYYFRU2g",
			"originalText": "We also have specific names for the first and the last node in the list. \nWe call the first node “HEAD” and the last node “TAIL”. \nAs you see above, tail node points to a null value, which means Linked Lists are “null terminated”. \nIn simpler words, this is how we know we are at the end of a Linked List.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "UV4zSctZg464M90mgal_r",
			"type": "rectangle",
			"x": -421.2707121939967,
