		{
			"id": "Ttl7uJUa",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -416.06017029986526,
			"y": 348.93533232354827,
			"width": 909.8831420389447,
			"height": 550,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dotted",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b0X",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 1344385326,
			"version": 149,
			"versionNonce": 544661941,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783350667405,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "A Linked List is a linear data structure consisted by a series of connected Nodes.\nElements (nodes) are not stored in contiguous memory locations (unlike arrays).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEach Node contains 2 properties:\n- Value: Holds the value / data for the Node.\n- Next (pointer): Holds a reference (pointer) to the next Node.",
			"rawText": "A Linked List is a linear data structure consisted by a series of connected Nodes. \nElements (nodes) are not stored in contiguous memory locations (unlike arrays).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEach Node contains 2 properties:\n- Value: Holds the value / data for the Node.\n- Next (pointer): Holds a reference (pointer) to the next Node.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "A Linked List is a linear data structure consisted by a series of connected Nodes. \nElements (nodes) are not stored in contiguous memory locations (unlike arrays).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEach Node contains 2 properties:\n- Value: Holds the value / data for the Node.\n- Next (pointer): Holds a reference (pointer) to the next Node.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
