			"seed": 1856434094,
			"version": 196,
			"versionNonce": 597445621,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783350667405,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "- O(1) Constant Time for Prepend: Inserting at the very beginning is instant. In an\nArray, inserting at index 0 forces every other element to shift right, costing O(n)\nlinear time.\n- True O(1) Insertions/Deletions (at known pointers): If you already have a pointer to a\nspecific node, inserting a new node after it, or deleting the node after it, is strictly\nO(1) constant time.\n- Dynamic Size: Memory allocation is done at runtime, node by node. No need to pre-\nallocate massive blocks of memory.\n- Efficient Splicing: You can take an entire sub-list and insert it into the middle of\nanother Linked List in O(1) time simply by updating two pointers, regardless of how long\nthe sub-list is.\n- Perfect for Queues and Deques: Linked Lists are naturally suited for First-In-First-\nOut (FIFO) queue implementations where you constantly add to the tail and remove from\nthe head without ever shifting elements.",
			"rawText": "- O(1) Constant Time for Prepend: Inserting at the very beginning is instant. In an Array, inserting at index 0 forces every other element to shift right, costing O(n) linear time.\n- True O(1) Insertions/Deletions (at known pointers): If you already have a pointer to a specific node, inserting a new node after it, or deleting the node after it, is strictly O(1) constant time.\n- Dynamic Size: Memory allocation is done at runtime, node by node. No need to pre-allocate massive blocks of memory.\n- Efficient Splicing: You can take an entire sub-list and insert it into the middle of another Linked List in O(1) time simply by updating two pointers, regardless of how long the sub-list is.\n- Perfect for Queues and Deques: Linked Lists are naturally suited for First-In-First-Out (FIFO) queue implementations where you constantly add to the tail and remove from the head without ever shifting elements.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "0t4tlg8b",
			"originalText": "- O(1) Constant Time for Prepend: Inserting at the very beginning is instant. In an Array, inserting at index 0 forces every other element to shift right, costing O(n) linear time.\n- True O(1) Insertions/Deletions (at known pointers): If you already have a pointer to a specific node, inserting a new node after it, or deleting the node after it, is strictly O(1) constant time.\n- Dynamic Size: Memory allocation is done at runtime, node by node. No need to pre-allocate massive blocks of memory.\n- Efficient Splicing: You can take an entire sub-list and insert it into the middle of another Linked List in O(1) time simply by updating two pointers, regardless of how long the sub-list is.\n- Perfect for Queues and Deques: Linked Lists are naturally suited for First-In-First-Out (FIFO) queue implementations where you constantly add to the tail and remove from the head without ever shifting elements.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
