			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783350667405,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "- O(n) Linear Time for Access: You lose Random Access. To get the 10th item, you must\nvisit items 1 through 9.\n- Memory Overhead: Every node requires extra memory to store the next reference.\n- Singly Linked Limits: In a standard Singly Linked List, you cannot traverse backward.\nIf you traverse past the node you needed, you must start entirely over from the head.\n-Terrible Cache Performance: As mentioned above, the scattered memory allocation\nresults in constant CPU cache misses, making traversals computationally expensive at\nthe hardware level.",
			"rawText": "- O(n) Linear Time for Access: You lose Random Access. To get the 10th item, you must visit items 1 through 9.\n- Memory Overhead: Every node requires extra memory to store the next reference.\n- Singly Linked Limits: In a standard Singly Linked List, you cannot traverse backward. If you traverse past the node you needed, you must start entirely over from the head.\n-Terrible Cache Performance: As mentioned above, the scattered memory allocation results in constant CPU cache misses, making traversals computationally expensive at the hardware level.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "tMyAW717",
			"originalText": "- O(n) Linear Time for Access: You lose Random Access. To get the 10th item, you must visit items 1 through 9.\n- Memory Overhead: Every node requires extra memory to store the next reference.\n- Singly Linked Limits: In a standard Singly Linked List, you cannot traverse backward. If you traverse past the node you needed, you must start entirely over from the head.\n-Terrible Cache Performance: As mentioned above, the scattered memory allocation results in constant CPU cache misses, making traversals computationally expensive at the hardware level.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
