		{
			"id": "CaSY49PB",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 703.6977986324159,
			"y": 4873.462961967574,
			"width": 1176.9984130859375,
			"height": 300,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 2,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b2W",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 353639093,
			"version": 696,
			"versionNonce": 1492899639,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783366276623,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Time Complexity: O(n) — Linear Time\n - Best Case (O(1): You are looking for index 0. The while loop never runs, and it instantly returns the \n   head.\n - Worst Case (O(n)): You are looking for the very last item in the list. The while loop must execute n \n   times, hopping from one node to the next until it reaches the end.\n - Average Case (O(n)): On average, you will be looking for an item somewhere in the middle. \n   mathematically, this takes O(n/2) steps. In Big-O notation, we drop the constants, leaving us with O(n).\n\nSpace Complexity: O(1) — Constant Space\n - No matter how massive the Linked List is (10 items or 10 million items), this method only ever creates \n   two temporary variables in memory: one integer (counter)  and one pointer reference (currentNode). \n   It does not duplicate the list.",
			"rawText": "Time Complexity: O(n) — Linear Time\n - Best Case (O(1): You are looking for index 0. The while loop never runs, and it instantly returns the \n   head.\n - Worst Case (O(n)): You are looking for the very last item in the list. The while loop must execute n \n   times, hopping from one node to the next until it reaches the end.\n - Average Case (O(n)): On average, you will be looking for an item somewhere in the middle. \n   mathematically, this takes O(n/2) steps. In Big-O notation, we drop the constants, leaving us with O(n).\n\nSpace Complexity: O(1) — Constant Space\n - No matter how massive the Linked List is (10 items or 10 million items), this method only ever creates \n   two temporary variables in memory: one integer (counter)  and one pointer reference (currentNode). \n   It does not duplicate the list.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "WcScwc6C",
			"originalText": "Time Complexity: O(n) — Linear Time\n - Best Case (O(1): You are looking for index 0. The while loop never runs, and it instantly returns the \n   head.\n - Worst Case (O(n)): You are looking for the very last item in the list. The while loop must execute n \n   times, hopping from one node to the next until it reaches the end.\n - Average Case (O(n)): On average, you will be looking for an item somewhere in the middle. \n   mathematically, this takes O(n/2) steps. In Big-O notation, we drop the constants, leaving us with O(n).\n\nSpace Complexity: O(1) — Constant Space\n - No matter how massive the Linked List is (10 items or 10 million items), this method only ever creates \n   two temporary variables in memory: one integer (counter)  and one pointer reference (currentNode). \n   It does not duplicate the list.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
