		{
			"id": "InJqVW9Y",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 3368.530751459676,
			"y": 4266.734914228578,
			"width": 1077.9986572265625,
			"height": 225,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b4g",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 143637431,
			"version": 854,
			"versionNonce": 358707161,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783371038847,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "\n1. Cache Downstream Reference: nextNode = currentNode.next;\n   Preserves access to the remaining sequence before modifying links.\n2. Pivot the Pointer: currentNode.next = previousNode;\n   Reverses the link path by directing the current node's pointer backward.\n3. Advance the Previous Tracker: previousNode = currentNode;\n   Steps the previous reference forward, setting the current node as the target for the next loop.\n4. Advance the Current Tracker: currentNode = nextNode;\n   Steps the execution focus forward into the cached downstream sequence.",
			"rawText": "\n1. Cache Downstream Reference: nextNode = currentNode.next;\n   Preserves access to the remaining sequence before modifying links.\n2. Pivot the Pointer: currentNode.next = previousNode;\n   Reverses the link path by directing the current node's pointer backward.\n3. Advance the Previous Tracker: previousNode = currentNode;\n   Steps the previous reference forward, setting the current node as the target for the next loop.\n4. Advance the Current Tracker: currentNode = nextNode;\n   Steps the execution focus forward into the cached downstream sequence.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "bottom",
			"containerId": "dzwneiwl",
			"originalText": "\n1. Cache Downstream Reference: nextNode = currentNode.next;\n   Preserves access to the remaining sequence before modifying links.\n2. Pivot the Pointer: currentNode.next = previousNode;\n   Reverses the link path by directing the current node's pointer backward.\n3. Advance the Previous Tracker: previousNode = currentNode;\n   Steps the previous reference forward, setting the current node as the target for the next loop.\n4. Advance the Current Tracker: currentNode = nextNode;\n   Steps the execution focus forward into the cached downstream sequence.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
