		{
			"id": "U7HP26w4",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 5767.396037924815,
			"y": 967.4770365984959,
			"width": 1022.9987182617188,
			"height": 175,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#e3fafc",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b5w",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 740662700,
			"version": 93,
			"versionNonce": 1225051796,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783375843706,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Time Complexity: O(n) (Linear Time)To ensure complete coverage, the execution path must scale\nin a direct 1:1 relationship with the number of elements ($n$) in the collection. If the\ncollection size doubles, the number of traversal operations doubles.\nSpace Complexity: O(1) (Constant Space)An iterative linear traversal only requires a fixed\nallocation of memory on the stack to maintain the tracking needle (e.g., an index integer\nvariable i or a node pointer reference currentNode), independent of the size of the data\nstructure.",
			"rawText": "Time Complexity: O(n) (Linear Time)To ensure complete coverage, the execution path must scale in a direct 1:1 relationship with the number of elements ($n$) in the collection. If the collection size doubles, the number of traversal operations doubles.\nSpace Complexity: O(1) (Constant Space)An iterative linear traversal only requires a fixed allocation of memory on the stack to maintain the tracking needle (e.g., an index integer variable i or a node pointer reference currentNode), independent of the size of the data structure.",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": "6DfagzTk",
			"originalText": "Time Complexity: O(n) (Linear Time)To ensure complete coverage, the execution path must scale in a direct 1:1 relationship with the number of elements ($n$) in the collection. If the collection size doubles, the number of traversal operations doubles.\nSpace Complexity: O(1) (Constant Space)An iterative linear traversal only requires a fixed allocation of memory on the stack to maintain the tracking needle (e.g., an index integer variable i or a node pointer reference currentNode), independent of the size of the data structure.",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
		{
			"id": "cuuL9ZJG",
			"type": "text",
			"x": 5762.720204758315,
			"y": 1213.8890456968434,
			"width": 1028.2955045120143,
			"height": 200,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "dashed",
			"roughness": 0,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b5x",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 852905516,
			"version": 263,
			"versionNonce": 1780826132,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1783376035336,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "Linear traversals serve as the baseline architecture for several mandatory operations:\n\n- Linear Search: Inspecting each element sequentially until a target value is matched or the\nboundary is reached (O(1) best case, O(n) worst case).\n- Aggregation: Accumulating values to compute global metrics like structural sums, counts, -\naverages, minimums, or maximums (always O(n)).\n- Deep Copying/Printing: Extracting payloads to replicate the structure or output its state\nto a console (O(n)).",
			"rawText": "Linear traversals serve as the baseline architecture for several mandatory operations:\n\n- Linear Search: Inspecting each element sequentially until a target value is matched or the boundary is reached (O(1) best case, O(n) worst case).\n- Aggregation: Accumulating values to compute global metrics like structural sums, counts, -averages, minimums, or maximums (always O(n)).\n- Deep Copying/Printing: Extracting payloads to replicate the structure or output its state to a console (O(n)).",
			"fontSize": 20,
			"fontFamily": 8,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "Linear traversals serve as the baseline architecture for several mandatory operations:\n\n- Linear Search: Inspecting each element sequentially until a target value is matched or the boundary is reached (O(1) best case, O(n) worst case).\n- Aggregation: Accumulating values to compute global metrics like structural sums, counts, -averages, minimums, or maximums (always O(n)).\n- Deep Copying/Printing: Extracting payloads to replicate the structure or output its state to a console (O(n)).",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"link": null
		},
